Z||000000||Dave85||10-17-1999||12:01 PM||||<BR>My temp. gauge is reading low but in traffic or at idle for a while the fan will come on like it should. I've checked the coolant level and replaced the thermostat. Should I replace the gauge or would it be the sender?||||reg||1
Z||000001||David||10-17-1999||02:35 PM||||Go for the sender first.  They usually go bad more often than a guage, plus they are cheaper and easier to replace.||||reg||1
